    {
      "id": "p1",
      "number": 1,
      "title": "Problem 1",
      "sourcePages": [
        3
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You have to tile a room that is two units wide and $N$ units long. You have with you two types of tiles: a rectangle that is one unit wide and two units long, and an L-shaped tile covering three square units. Here are pictures of the two types of tiles."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "src": "figures/zio2009-p1-tiles.png",
          "alt": "The two tile types: a 1 × 2 rectangle and an L-shaped tile covering three squares.",
          "caption": null,
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "You are allowed to rotate the tiles when you lay them. You have an infinite supply of both types of tiles. However, your architect is from Nauru and is a believer in the Polynesian system of tiling called Batlar Guntu which forbids any corner where four tiles meet."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "For instance, here are some ways to tile a 2 × 4 room. The first three are consistent with the Batlar Guntu system while the fourth tiling is not."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "src": "figures/zio2009-p1-ways.png",
          "alt": "Four ways to tile a 2 × 4 room. The first three obey the Batlar Guntu rule; the fourth has four tiles meeting at a corner and does not.",
          "caption": null,
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Your task is to calculate the number of different ways a room can be tiled without violating the principles of Batlar Guntu. For instance, a 2 × 3 room can be tiled in 5 different ways, as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "src": "figures/zio2009-p1-ways3.png",
          "alt": "The five ways to tile a 2 × 3 room.",
          "caption": null,
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Calculate the number of different ways of tiling rooms of the following sizes."
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
        {
