    {
      "id": "p2",
      "number": 2,
      "title": "Problem 2",
      "sourcePages": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "ZIngO is ZIO Solitaire for the New Generation, played on an $N$ × $N$ square grid of numbers. You start by placing a token on any square of the grid. Then, in each turn, you move the token either one square to the right or one square down. The game ends when you move the token off the edge of the board."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Each square of the grid contains a number. You start with a score of zero. Whenever the token lands on a square, including the square you begin with, you add its value to your current score. The object of the game is to score as many points as possible."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "For example, given the grid below, you can score 5 − 2 + 4 + 7 − 3 + 4 = 15 points by placing the token initially on the 5 in the first column, and then moving right, down, right, right, down, down. This is the maximum score possible for this game."
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "src": "figures/zio2009-p2-example.png",
          "alt": "A 5 × 5 grid of numbers with the path 5, −2, 4, 7, −3, 4 marked by arrows.",
          "caption": null,
          "source": null
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Compute the maximum possible ZIngO score for each of the following grids."
        }
      ],
